module

public import CFSGCorollary.TwoGenerated.Basic
public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.CFSG.Classification
import CFSGCorollary.Alternating.TwoGenerated
import CFSGCorollary.Cyclic
import CFSGCorollary.LieType.TwoGenerated
import CFSGCorollary.Sporadic.TwoGenerated

/-!
# Every group on TauCeti's list of finite simple groups is generated by two elements

TauCeti's `TauCeti.ClassificationStatement` states the classification of finite simple groups:
every finite simple group is isomorphic to `i.Group` for some index `i : TauCeti.CFSGIndex`. We
prove that every group on this list is generated by two elements, treating each entry:

* cyclic groups of prime order are generated by one element (`CFSGCorollary.twoGenerated_cyclic`);
* for `n ≥ 5`, the alternating group `Aₙ` is generated by an explicit 3-cycle and an `n`-cycle or
  `(n-1)`-cycle, using Jordan's theorem on primitive groups containing a 3-cycle
  (`CFSGCorollary.twoGenerated_alternating`);
* the groups of Lie type are generated by two elements built from root subgroups and Weyl group
  representatives as in R. Steinberg (1962), and the Tits group is an explicit two-generated
  permutation group (`CFSGCorollary.twoGenerated_lie`);
* the sporadic groups are realised by AxiomMath/CFSG as explicit two-generated permutation or
  matrix groups, and the Monster through its `Y₄₄₃` presentation
  (`CFSGCorollary.twoGenerated_sporadic`).

## Main results

* `CFSGCorollary.twoGenerated_cfsgIndex`: every group on TauCeti's list is two-generated.

`Comparator/Solution.lean`, outside this library, deduces that every finite simple group is
generated by two elements, first assuming the classification and then using AxiomMath/CFSG's
proof of it; nothing in the `CFSGCorollary` library imports that proof.

## References

* [R. Steinberg, *Generators for simple groups*, Canad. J. Math. 14 (1962) 277–283][Steinberg1962]
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace CFSGCorollary

/-- Every group on TauCeti's list of finite simple groups is two-generated. -/
theorem twoGenerated_cfsgIndex (index : TauCeti.CFSGIndex)
    [Finite index.Group] [IsSimpleGroup index.Group] : TwoGenerated index.Group := by
  cases index with
  | cyclic p _ => exact twoGenerated_cyclic p
  | alternating n h => exact twoGenerated_alternating n h
  | lie d => exact twoGenerated_lie d
  | sporadic s => exact twoGenerated_sporadic s

end CFSGCorollary
